</surname><given-names>WI</given-names></name><name><surname>Collins</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><article-title>Gut motor function: immunological control in enteric infection and inflammation</article-title><source>Clin Exp Immunol</source><year>2006</year><volume>143</volume><fpage>389</fpage><lpage>397</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16487236</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Akiho</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Khan</surname><given-names>WI</given-names></name><name><surname>Al Kaabi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Blennerhassett</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Deng</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Collins</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><article-title>Cytokine modulation of muscarinic receptors in the murine intestine</article-title><source>Am J Physiol Gastrointest Liver Physiol</source><year>2007</year><volume>293</volume><fpage>G250</fpage><lpage>G255</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17431212</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Akiho</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Deng</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Blennerhassett</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Kanbayashi</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Collins</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><article-title>Mechanisms underlying the maintenance of muscle hypercontractility in a model of postinfective gut dysfunction</article-title><source>Gastroenterology</source><year>2005</year><volume>129</volume><fpage>131</fpage><lpage>141</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16012943</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Vallance</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name><name><surname>Radojevic</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Hogaboam</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Deng</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Gauldie</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Collins</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><article-title>IL-4 gene transfer to the small bowel serosa leads to intestinal inflammation and smooth muscle hyperresponsiveness</article-title><source>Am J Physiol Gastrointest Liver Physiol</source><year>2007</year><volume>292</volume><fpage>G385</fpage><lpage>G394</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17215437</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Vaali</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Puumalainen</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Lehto</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Wolff</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Rita</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Alenius</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Palosuo</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><article-title>Murine model of food allergy after epicutaneous sensitization: role of mucosal mast cell protease-1</article-title><source>Scand J Gastroenterol</source><year>2006</year><volume>41</volume><fpage>1405</fpage><lpage>1413</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17101571</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Moreels</surname><given-names>TG</given-names></name><name><surname>De Man</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name><name><surname>De Winter</surname><given-names>BY</given-names></name><name><surname>Herman</surname><given-names>AG</given-names></name><name><surname>Pelckmans</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><article-title>How to express pharmacological contractions of the inflamed rat intestine</article-t